We can form a kagamimochi by placing mochi $A$ on top of mochi $B$ if and only if $A \le \frac{B}{2}$.
We need to select $2K$ mochi to form $K$ pairs. Each pair $(A, B)$ must satisfy $A \le B/2$. We want to maximize $K$.

Let's denote the sizes of the mochi as $A_1 \le A_2 \le \dots \le A_N$.
We want to choose $K$ pairs $(A_{i_1}, B_{i_1}), (A_{i_2}, B_{i_2}), \dots, (A_{i_K}, B_{i_K})$ such that for each $j$, $A_{i_j} \le B_{i_j} / 2$, and all indices $i_1, \dots, i_K$ and $j_1, \dots, j_K$ are distinct.
